WEBVTT

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.920
This is quite a contest.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.650
Which one?

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.660
Why, both, of course.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.990
This is such fun.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.770
I feel so alive right now.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:02.010
<b>A 7.62 mm Mirage</b>

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:06.520
<b>Days ago, in Northern Africa</b>

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.890
Here you are.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.030
Did you need anything else?

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.030
Hi!

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:34.580
You're always here around 
this time of day, aren't you?

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.690
That's 'cause I know I'll
 run into a cutie like you.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:39.060
Oh, you...

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.820
<i>Her injuries are relatively minor 
and not thought to be life-threatening.</i>

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:08.370
<i>So far, no one has claimed 
responsibility for the attack.</i>

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:13.200
<i>The scene of the shooting was crowded 
and it is believed that this was...</i>

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:13.200
Looks like you weren't the 
only one after that waitress.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.950
<i>a factor in concealing 
the gunman's presence.</i>

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.760
What a damn mess.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.330
I hate that she was targeted because of me.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:22.830
So much for my plan to seduce her.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.320
<i>A video has been posted on the website,</i>

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:29.220
<i>believed to show the type of 
ammunition the gunman used.</i>

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.130
<i>The gold-colored shell casing seen here...</i>

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.230
D4 is a chess move, you see.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.530
Old Zylberstein's calling me out.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.250
You mean, the psychotic rich guy?

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:40.910
What're you gonna do, Lupin?

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.100
I'm totally wiped out 
after our last big job.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.470
I don't have the energy to humor the elderly.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:49.240
I figured as much.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.220
In that case, I'm gonna 
get some shuteye, too.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.000
<i>This time, it looks like an officer 
on patrol has been shot in the arm.</i>

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:07.350
<i>We now have multiple shootings, and 
no statement from those responsible.</i>

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.010
<i>What could their motive be for these attacks?</i>

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:15.030
Lupin III has accepted my invitation.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:19.650
I'm expecting great things from you.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.890
Well, it's been a while, Young Lupin.

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:04.560
About three years, I think.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.780
Glad to see you're still in good health.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.270
So we're playing chess this time?

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:15.280
Well? What are the stakes?

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.700
Hm, let's say a million euros.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.740
I'm counting on you, partner.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:31.780
<i>The police have searched the scene 
of the shooting thoroughly,</i>

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.490
<i>but have yet to turn up 
any meaningful leads.</i>

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.170
Hey, Jigen...

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.440
Ever hear of a sniper who 
goes by the name of Mirage?

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:47.500
Looks like the old man's 
been hunting for hired help.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:52.490
Mirage... I haven't heard 
that name in a long time.

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:55.500
Used to be a sniper. A mercenary.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.720
We've fought side by side a few times.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:01.070
I see. This Mirage must be the
 one behind all the shootings.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:07.090
Lupin. Mirage is a crack shot.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.990
If you don't take this seriously, you're 
gonna end up with a hole in your head.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.460
It'll be fine.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:18.010
I've got an even better sniper 
watching my back, after all.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:22.230
Maybe I'll help you track down this 
sniper friend who's got your back.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:25.510
Aw, Jigen, that's ice cold, man!

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:28.340
Besides, you'll find him in the bathroom. 
Just look in the mirror!

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:31.470
He's an old— uh, <i>dashing</i> 
young fellow with a beard!

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:33.440
Hey, don't bother correcting yourself!

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:34.680
So... you in?

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:40.600
Just so you know, I didn't bring my rifle 
since I'm supposed to be on vacation.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.510
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:06:58.790 --> 00:06:59.860
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:02.950
<i>Where, oh, where?</i>

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:04.570
<i>Bingo.</i>

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:12.080
<i>No... Mirage wouldn't be that stupid.</i>

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:21.590
Dammit.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.600
That's right, Mirage.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.600
Looks like you and me have the first dance!

00:07:57.480 --> 00:08:01.260
You really wanna see me die that badly?

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:04.330
We're not gonna make it 
easy for you, you realize.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:12.270
I'm positively atingle at the prospect 
of seeing your head explode.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.200
Like a watermelon.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.640
You never learn.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.650
By the way, young man...

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.850
Did you know Mirage was a woman?

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:42.680
Oh dear. Friends keeping 
secrets from each other...

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:47.180
Maybe he was scared I'd steal 
her out from under his nose.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:57.620
You know, that girl...

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:05.430
She became a civil war refugee after 
her parents were killed in front of her.

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:08.290
So how did she end up as a sniper?

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.910
You could call it a twist of fate.

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:18.990
Her refugee camp was attacked by some 
vicious insurgent guerrillas, you see.

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:20.190
And?

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:26.880
She picked up the rifle 
of a dead French soldier

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.380
who had been attempting to protect the camp.

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:36.820
She was one hell of a hunter, 
you see. Took after her father.

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:37.970
I get what you're saying.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.990
She grew up to be a superlative sniper.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:46.330
The kind that is feared by 
 enemies and allies alike.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:49.490
That's when she got her nickname: Mirage.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:53.110
People were getting shot by an illusion, huh?

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:58.270
When the civil war finally ended, 
she became a gun for hire to make a living.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:03.610
I actually hired her a few times 
when she was first starting out.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:04.610
Hey, Gramps...

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.960
You're leaving out the 
most important bit of info.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.780
Oh? And what might that be?

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:13.010
Is she a fox?

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:21.030
Oh, yes! Your beloved Fujiko Mine
 pales in comparison.

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:22.510
Really?

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.030
What's this?

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:39.140
<i>HEIAP rounds?!</i>

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.290
<i>Gotcha.</i>

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:20.340
She predicted where I was going to be...

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.990
How'd she know?

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.950
Damn. Moving with the times, huh?

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:38.510
This is quite a contest.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:40.470
Which one?

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:43.160
Why, both, of course.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:48.470
This is such fun.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:56.190
I feel so alive right now.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:18.730
Never thought you'd quit before me.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:27.350
I have a new fight now. 
One I'm really excited about.

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:31.900
D'you think you'll be able to manage?

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:34.340
Thanks for the concern, Jigen.

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:37.140
But I'll be okay.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:42.360
I think I'll be stronger than ever 
if I'm fighting for someone else's sake.

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:47.630
Well, I've never been serious about 
protecting anyone other than myself.

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:49.380
So I wouldn't know.

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:55.400
That thing must be heavy...

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:59.120
Want me to take it off your hands?

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:05.840
I'll carry the weight.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:06.940
All right.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:13.010
I think I only made it this far because 
I've never gone up against you, Jigen.

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:17.240
And now, I'm relieved I never have to fight you.

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:19.630
The feeling's mutual.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.530
Well... we'll probably never meet again...

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.540
Yeah. It's probably for the best.

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:41.050
<i>What exactly are you protecting 
by coming back, Mirage?</i>

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.280
Checkmate, I think.

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:57.690
Not yet.

00:14:58.050 --> 00:14:59.740
I mean, for them.

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:08.260
Damn it all. This makes me 
wish I'd quit smoking.

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:19.860
A ricochet?

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.780
Looks like your luck ran out, Gramps.

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:26.670
Why?!

00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:30.110
Dammit!

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:40.150
King... to F5....

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:44.740
King to F7.

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:47.430
Pawn to F3!

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:51.370
I resign, Gramps.

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:53.630
Got you!

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:05.310
Mirage!

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:13.720
What the hell?

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:17.430
But why? That rubble should've crushed you.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:19.900
I shot it up.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:40.320
And who are you supposed to—

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:41.740
Mirage's daughter, am I right?

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:47.650
Then... where is she?

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:50.790
My mother's still fighting. She's very sick.

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:54.390
She won't get better unless 
we get her to a hospital in Europe.

00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:56.590
But we don't have that kind of money.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:18:01.270
So, when you heard about this job,
 you applied for it yourself?

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:03.020
Cut the crap.

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:07.840
Mirage left the battlefield 
so she could raise you right!

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:13.270
And now you waltz straight back into it, 
just to make a bit of cash?

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:14.570
Shut up!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:17.530
Even though we were living in peacetime, 
my mother taught me how to fight!

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:22.540
She told me if I ever had a reason to fight,
 she wouldn't stand in my way!

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:26.780
Well, <i>this</i> is that time! If I don't fight 
for her now, when <i>will</i> I take up arms?!

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:30.580
If you think <i>you</i> can make her better,

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.340
then do so!

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.790
All right, settle down, you two.

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:38.810
The fight's over now.

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:40.100
No, it's not!

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:42.060
I need that money!

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:44.520
And I'll provide you with 
what you need soon enough.

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:48.530
Before you refuse, 
I'm not talking about charity.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:50.800
I lost to this old timer at chess.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:54.560
So you get the pot. No small loss, believe me.

00:18:56.550 --> 00:19:00.060
Your mom was a hell of a shot.

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:03.510
And I'm gonna butt in 
one last time before I go.

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:05.720
You're not cut out for this work.

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:08.950
No matter how hard you try,

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:12.090
you're never gonna be 
the sniper your mom was.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:18.080
It's not too late. Turn your
 hand to something else.

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:22.060
Stop chasing a mirage.

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:27.520
Since I didn't kill you, I'm taking this.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:31.600
I don't think you'll be needing it again.

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:35.460
Tell your mom you got rid of it.

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.610
I know she'll understand.

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:54.130
You sure you wanna let 
the old coot off the hook?

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.260
Once he's feeling better, I'll play him again.

00:19:57.260 --> 00:19:59.110
Well, count me out.

00:19:59.110 --> 00:20:01.760
Today shaved five years off my life.

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:07.920
You saved my butt, Jigen.

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:09.780
I appreciate it.

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:14.360
That girl... If she'd kept at it...

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:16.920
If she'd kept at it...

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:21.870
I think she might've become an 
even better sniper than her mom.

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:27.690
That thing looks heavy. Want me to carry it?

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:38.350
I'll bear the weight.

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:18.650
Daisuke Jigen here.

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:23.620
Looks like another thief has made off with 
our score before we could get our hands on it.

00:22:23.620 --> 00:22:26.410
Wait, what the hell? It's Zenigata!

00:22:26.410 --> 00:22:31.020
From cop to criminal... 
That's quite a career move.

00:22:31.020 --> 00:22:34.030
And you're shockingly good at it, too.

00:22:34.030 --> 00:22:37.590
Maybe you're better suited 
to be working on our side, pal.

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:45.040
<b>Zenigata, Gentleman Thief</b>

00:22:38.050 --> 00:22:40.140
Next time: Zenigata, Gentleman Thief.

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:43.480
Good grief. Even Zenigata's crooked now.
